# Line endings are LF everywhere, in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# This is not a style preference. Two things in this repository compare bytes:
# check_house_rules.py requires a note's assets/<tool>.py to be a byte copy of
# _shared/tools/<tool>.py, and the published assets archive is expected to hold
# the same bytes the repository does. The Git for Windows installer sets
# core.autocrlf=true at system scope, so a plain clone on Windows rewrites the
# working tree to CRLF. Any file a script then rewrites with LF stops matching
# its checked-out counterpart, and the byte comparison fails for a reason that
# has nothing to do with the file's content. Pinning eol=lf here overrides
# core.autocrlf whatever the machine is configured to do, so the check means
# what it says on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Built artifacts and vendor binaries: no normalisation, no eol conversion.
# The firmware .hex and .bin files are shipped to readers as the vendor
# released them, so nothing may rewrite a byte of them.
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.bin binary
*.hex binary
